Then, the functions $\{x_k(t)\}_{k=1}^{2m-1}$ defined by
\begin{equation}
\begin{dcases}
& q_k(t)=1+x_{2k-2}(t)+x_{2k-1}(t) \q (k=1, \ldots, m), \\
& e_k(t)=x_{2k-1}(t)x_{2k}(t) \q (k=1, \ldots, m-1), \\
& x_0(t)\equiv 0
\end{dcases}
\label{eq:Miura}
\end{equation}
satisfy the Lotka-Volterra equation \eqref{eq:LV}.
